On Oct 12, 11:16 pm, Andrew <buttercat.apocaly...@gmail.com> wrote:
> What are your personal best ring choices, ignoring any which give
> intrinsics that can be gotten by other means? What do you use in your
> ascention kit?
>

Conflict #1, it's the only almost "must have" for the ascension run.

There are only 3 other rings I use much at all by this point:

I usually wind up with levitation via ring, from air through water.
From the sanctum up, teleport control is incredibly useful and I often
have to use the ring since getting it from tengu//Rodney is hit or
miss.  But once you're on the Planes you can ditch it.
Free action's not that useful, but there's not too much else to do
with that slot and it can save you from one very rare death that can't
be prevented easily in other ways (thrown potion of paralysis, most
likely to cause death when surrounded on Astral).

So I usually ascend wearing conflict + free action, though I wouldn't
normally waste a wish on the latter unless I have tons of wishes to
spare by the time I'm heading to the Planes.

> Also, what's better, increase damage or increase accuracy? Or
> protection?

Damage and protection have some value early, but all 3 are pretty low-
value by the late game.

Increase accuracy is almost completely useless once you've maxed luck,
since you'll almost never miss anything from then on.
Increase damage is pretty useless by the time you're on the ascension
run, since you're rarely engaging in combat and when you do your
damage output is normally pretty massive already.
Protection depends on the value, but normally even a fairly quick run
has put together good enough AC without needing it (conduct games
excepted).


